  "text": "anya: quick accessibility check for the compact model selector in the sidebar. NVDA on Windows reads the list, but when you arrow between items the selected state isn't exposed.\nben: saw this too. NVDA just says the label, no selected/checked announcement. tabindex looks fine though.\nkevin: dug into the DOM: selector is an unordered list <ul> of <li><button>. we use .selected class visually but no aria-current/aria-checked. also role semantics unclear: is this single-select or multi-select?\njess: it's single-select: pick one model to preview. selected should be conveyed as current. aria-current=\"true\" on the selected item would help screen readers announce it.\nanya: also noticed keyboard focus outline is 1px and almost invisible at 2x zoom. contrast for focus ring with the dark theme is borderline.\naria-bot: scan results (compact-selector): failures: 2 (missing aria-current, low focus indicator contrast). details: https://ci.internal/reports/a11y/1876504321\nben: repro steps with NVDA:\n```\n1) Start NVDA\n2) Open Console -> left sidebar -> Compact selector\n3) Press Down arrow to move through items\n4) Note announcements\n```\nben: NVDA mode matters: browse mode vs focus mode. With buttons we should be in focus mode, but NVDA sometimes stays in browse mode if markup isn't semantic.\nkevin: proposal: change list markup to role=\"listbox\" and items role=\"option\" with aria-selected=\"true\" for the chosen item. listbox/option maps nicely to arrow-key navigation.\njess: listbox semantics are good for single-select and will give proper arrow navigation. downside: we need to implement roving tabindex (only the active option has tabindex=0, others -1) or NVDA will skip.\nanya: alternative: keep buttons but add aria-current=\"true\" on selected and ensure focus lands on the button when opening sidebar. I worry about listbox requiring larger change.\nben: for minimal fix: 1) add aria-current/aria-pressed-like attribute 2) ensure focus moves to selected item on open 3) bump focus outline to 3px and use #FFD54F on dark theme so WCAG 2.1 contrast >= 3:1 for focus ring against panel.\nkevin: sample patch I tested:\n```\n<li role=\"option\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">GPT-4o | <span class=\"meta\">fast</span></li>\n<li role=\"option\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">Mistral | <span class=\"meta\">cheap</span></li>\n```\nand JS to manage roving tabindex on keydown ArrowDown/ArrowUp.\njess: also add aria-live polite container for model load status: \"Model loaded: GPT-4o\" \u2014 otherwise screen reader users don't get feedback when switching.\nanya: acceptance criteria for ticket:\n- NVDA announces selected option when using arrow keys\n- Focus ring visible at 2x zoom and meets contrast\n- Screen reader hears model load confirmation via aria-live\n- Unit tests for keyboard navigation & aria attributes\naria-bot: created ticket INS-5209, linked scan, priority P2, assignee @kevin. ETA 5d.\nben: noted a flaky behavior: when the sidebar is toggled open by click, focus is on the toggle button, not the selected option. need to set focus programmatically after open animation completes.\nkevin: will add small delay or animationend handler. also will add an e2e NVDA run script in our accessibility pipeline so we catch regressions.\njess: for copy: change visible selected hint from \"Selected\" to \"Selected \u2014 active\" so it reads clearer in some screen readers that read punctuation differently.\nanya: good call. small PR later today. I'll attach NVDA screencap and a short video of arrow nav.\nben: will verify on Windows 10 + NVDA 2024.3 and mac VoiceOver for parity.\nkevin: pushing branch now, ping when CI passes.\naria-bot: INS-5209 updated: branch pushed, a11y-e2e queued.\nanya: thanks all, merging notes into the design doc. closing the thread. :seedling:"
